// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
//
// Range Baseline Content — Epic #266, Phase 1.
//
// Real news websites + RSS feeds layered under the synthetic Range feed. An
// org-level catalog of BaselineWebsites (each with an optional RssFeed) is
// curated by instructors; each exercise explicitly enables which catalog
// websites are "live" inside it via ExerciseWebsiteConfig (explicit opt-in).
// A server-side fetcher (range-svc-worker) polls feeds, sanitizes HTML, and
// persists BaselineArticles; participants browse + full-text-search them.
//
// State-changing RPCs emit a paired audit envelope in the same tx as the
// domain write (platform/proto/CONVENTIONS.md §2). Subjects use the shared
// audit_subject() form (range. prefix stripped, first dot -> underscore),
// matching every existing range audit subject:
//   CreateWebsite       -> audit.range.baseline_website_created
//   UpdateWebsite       -> audit.range.baseline_website_updated
//   DeleteWebsite       -> audit.range.baseline_website_deleted
//   SyncFeed            -> audit.range.baseline_feed_synced
//   SetWebsiteEnabled   -> audit.range.baseline_website_config_set
//   BatchEnableWebsites -> audit.range.baseline_website_config_set (one per site)
//   CreateArticle       -> audit.range.baseline_article_created
//   UpdateArticle       -> audit.range.baseline_article_updated
//   DeleteArticle       -> audit.range.baseline_article_deleted
//   BulkArticleAction   -> audit.range.baseline_article_bulk_actioned
// (GenerateArticle is a stateless LLM draft — no persistence, no audit.)
// (The fetcher's business subjects range.baseline.poll.* / range.baseline.fetch.*
// and the worker-side audit.range.baseline_articles_fetched are documented in
// the worker phase; only the handler-side audit subjects are contracted here.)

